## Key Findings

### ✅ Authority Leakage: ZERO violations
The `authorityScope` backfill and [filterPhasesByAuthorityScope()](file:///c:/Users/aravi/Documents/AI_LLM/projects/exact-screenshot/src/shared/filterByJurisdiction.ts#184-202) pipeline are working correctly. No TRUST tasks leak into PROBATE roadmaps and no PROBATE tasks leak into TRUST roadmaps across any state.

### ⚠️ 3 Tasks Still Missing `authorityScope`
These 3 tasks appear across every state and lack explicit `authorityScope`:

| Task ID | Impact |
|---|---|
| `validate_venue_authority` | 153 violations across all states |
| `screen_fiduciary_eligibility` | 153 violations across all states |
| `identify_protected_persons_and_representation` | 153 violations across all states |

### ⚠️ `file_affidavit` Has Unresolved Template Tokens
The `file_affidavit` task contains raw `{{smallEstateThreshold}}` / `{{smallEstateTerm}}` template tokens that are not being resolved at the hardcoded-task level. They are resolved at render time by [applyStateRuleTokens()](file:///c:/Users/aravi/Documents/AI_LLM/projects/exact-screenshot/server/services/roadmapService.ts#121-128) in the DB path, but the static audit catches them pre-render.

### ⚠️ `monitor_creditor_claim_period` Contains Generic Wording
The task `monitor_creditor_claim_period` includes the phrase `"varies by state"` in 47 of 51 states. States with explicit creditor windows (GA, MN, NJ, OH) have state-specific overrides that suppress this.

### ⚠️ NY Cross-State Contamination
NY roadmaps contain 9 instances of CA-specific patterns (`IAEA`, `Notice of Proposed Action`, `Sale Confirmation Order`) leaking through `sell_property` and related tasks. These likely come from task `stateOverrides` that aren't fully stripping CA terminology for NY.

---

## Recommended Single Architectural Fix

> **Implement a centralized `StatuteBindingService`** that resolves all state-specific text at render time from the structured `STATE_RULES` registry, eliminating hardcoded statute references in task definitions. Combined with **making `authorityScope` required (non-optional)** on [PhaseTask](file:///c:/Users/aravi/Documents/AI_LLM/projects/exact-screenshot/src/config/settlementPhases.ts#13-112), this would eliminate the two largest violation classes (~60% reduction).

